# Auth for the ntfy bus server.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.claude/.env (preferred for bus creds — low-stakes tier)
# and fill in the values. Then: chmod 600 ~/.claude/.env
#
# The Send/CheckInbox workflows source both ~/.env and ~/.claude/.env, so either
# location works. Convention: bus credentials live in ~/.claude/.env. High-value
# keys (cloud, financial) live in ~/.env.
#
# These values are SHARED across all agents on the same bus today — one ntfy user
# is provisioned, every host uses the same pair.
# Per-agent identity is carried in the Title routing convention (SENDER→RECIPIENT),
# NOT in HTTP Basic auth. If per-agent ACLs become useful later, ntfy supports
# per-user/per-topic access control — set that up server-side and rotate.

NTFY_USERNAME=
NTFY_PASSWORD=
